      "title": "Control Plane Policing (CoPP) Guard & Interpretation Notice",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 6 },
      "id": 7,
      "options": {
        "content": "> 🛡️ **Control Plane Policing (CoPP) Guard Active**\n>\n> In modern enterprise and carrier backbones, core routing engines prioritize transit data-plane packets and aggressively rate-limit or drop ICMP `Time Exceeded` generation generated by their control plane CPUs.\n>\n> **Operational Invariant:** An intermediate hop showing timeouts (`*`) or high loss is **non-impairing** if downstream hops or the target destination are healthy (Loss < 20%). Nawari classifies these hops as `TIMEOUT_COPP` (CoPP Rate-Limited) and strictly omits synthetic RTT metrics, preventing spurious alarms and false ticket escalations to transit carriers.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.6.0",
      "title": "CoPP Guard Architectural Interpretation",
      "type": "text"
    },
